    <string name="glutton_help">How to play</string>
    <string name="glutton_rules">Drag anywhere to roll, let go to brake.\n\nEverything smaller than you is swallowed. Food piles up in a few rich corners and is thin elsewhere: look for them, they move as you grow. Bites close to your own size (green halo) make you grow fastest and show their name. Your stomach digests at its own pace: gulping a whole street at once does not make you a giant in a second.\n\nWhatever is too big to swallow blocks the way: go round it. Find the way out of the house, then eat your street, the town, the countryside, the mountains, the Earth, the solar system, the stars, the Milky Way and finally the whole universe. Your own house, the Earth and the Milky Way end up on the menu too.\n\nRobot vacuums, police cars, tornadoes, hurricanes and planets bump you while you are small and make you spit out your last bites: just swallow them again. Once you outgrow them, they are lunch.\n\nVacuum! pulls in everything in reach and stuns what moves.\n\nJourney: no clock, your time to swallow the universe is the record. Hunger: one minute on the clock. Growing wins a little time back, but never quite as much as passes, and hourglasses add a few seconds: get as big as you can before it runs out.</string>
